  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The actual conflict and the devastating effects on livelihoods, communities and businesses ask for the reorientation of the initial Strategic Plan that the Federation of Palestinian Chambers of Commerce, Industry and Agriculture (FPCCIA) has developed in the past biennium with ILO support.  One of the areas identified in the Strategic Plan was the capacity of the Federation to conduct research and advocacy campaigns on behalf of its members. In the actual situation, the Federation and its members need to reorient their capacities on how to conduct research, surveys, polls and communicate effectively, in particular on the impact that the actual conflict is having on business in Gaza and West Bank.  
This activity is part of the actual ILO Emergency response plan that includes additional support through recovery schemes via direct interventions and also partnerships with the Government where the Federation will be asked to intervene and provide informed arguments. 
The establishment of the Enterprise Support and Advocacy Unit (ESAU) within PFCCIA will provide Micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs) with customized technical assistance and employ data-driven analysis to champion policy reforms that nurture business growth.</narrative>
  </description>
